# Superpowers docs lifecycle

**This rule is always on.** It overrides Superpowers defaults that open a new dated file every time.

## Default: revise in place

1. Read `docs/superpowers/README.md` before any design write.
2. The living spec is **`docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-ue-mview-maplibre-design.md`** (UE dual viewport + mview shell + MapLibre + named pipe). New requirements on that product are a new `§` on that file.
3. Put **`Status:`** on the first metadata line when you edit it. Refresh the date when merging.
4. Open plans under `docs/superpowers/plans/`. Diagrams under `docs/superpowers/diagrams/`.
5. Keep `docs/superpowers/README.md` as a **short table**. Do not rebuild a full inventory in `docs/README.md`.

## When a new dated spec is allowed

Only if it is a **new top-level subsystem** with no row that can own it, and the new file says which living file was considered and why a `§` merge is impossible.

Do **not** open smartgis umbrellas (map2d frame, scene3d, plugin host, GDAL, legacy MFC). Those trees are not in this repo.

## Don’t

- Don’t add a dated twin that only restates the living GIS spec.
- Don’t archive the living spec while the topic is still open.
- Don’t ask the user to pick an umbrella when this file already owns desktop GIS.

## Diagrams

When a `§` or plan **locks architecture**, ship HTML under `docs/superpowers/diagrams/` in the same change. See `design-html-diagrams.mdc`.
